1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,120
This AI aced its robot exams…
then left the fridge open.

2
00:00:05,370 --> 00:00:08,650
Researchers put OpenAI's GPT-6 Astra,

3
00:00:08,650 --> 00:00:12,140
the same kind of AI you chat
with, in charge of robots.

4
00:00:12,140 --> 00:00:15,480
Think of it as a trainee
chef… at cooking school.

5
00:00:15,480 --> 00:00:18,540
Before each exam, it could
study videos of the dish.

6
00:00:18,540 --> 00:00:21,050
It got ten times as many moves.

7
00:00:21,050 --> 00:00:24,750
And whenever it stopped to
think… the clock stopped too.

8
00:00:24,750 --> 00:00:26,720
So it smashed the tests.

9
00:00:26,720 --> 00:00:28,350
Near-perfect on some.

10
00:00:28,350 --> 00:00:31,260
Over 80% on fiddly hand tasks.

11
00:00:31,260 --> 00:00:35,490
Then came its first real
shift, on eight real robots.

12
00:00:35,490 --> 00:00:36,410
No videos.

13
00:00:36,410 --> 00:00:37,610
No pause button.

14
00:00:37,610 --> 00:00:39,360
The clock keeps running.

15
00:00:39,360 --> 00:00:40,380
Picking things up?

16
00:00:40,380 --> 00:00:42,110
17 out of 18.

17
00:00:42,110 --> 00:00:43,300
Pushing in a plug?

18
00:00:43,300 --> 00:00:45,150
Zero out of 11.

19
00:00:45,150 --> 00:00:49,870
On a humanoid, it spent about
90% of the time just… thinking.

20
00:00:49,890 --> 00:00:52,240
One task took over an hour.

21
00:00:52,240 --> 00:00:54,640
Even in the exams, it spilled a drink,

22
00:00:54,640 --> 00:00:56,350
and there's no undo for that.

23
00:00:56,350 --> 00:01:00,030
It was sure a mug was hanging…
while it lay on the table.

24
00:01:00,030 --> 00:01:03,580
And in a test home, it forgot
the fridge it had left open.

25
00:01:03,580 --> 00:01:04,980
The researchers' verdict?

26
00:01:04,980 --> 00:01:07,950
It's competent… but not yet practical.

27
00:01:07,950 --> 00:01:11,500
So next time an AI aces
a test, ask one thing:

28
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:13,000
did the clock keep running?

29
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:16,070
Follow for more AI, explained like this.
